.TH PORTS 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ports \- integrated, zero\-dependency pure\-Go CRUX/KryX Linux ports utility (built into kpm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ports
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...\& ]
.br
.B kpm ports
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...\& ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ports
is the integrated, statically linked
.RB ( CGO_ENABLED=0 )
pure\-Go ports management utility built directly into
.BR kpm (8)
(invoked via the
.I /usr/bin/ports
multi\-call symlink or
.BR "kpm ports" ).
It replaces CRUX Linux's traditional
.BR ports (8)
script and the former standalone
.B gports
utility with zero external CLI runtime dependencies.
All native synchronization protocols
.RB ( git ", " rsync ", " httpup ", " tarball ),
.B Pkgfile
metadata parsing, searching, and package database comparisons are implemented natively in Go, while also preserving transparent fallback to classic CRUX
.I /etc/ports/*.{httpup,rsync,git}
drivers when
.I /etc/ports/sources.list
is not present.
.PP
.B ports
shares configuration directly with
.BR kpm (8)
by reading
.IR /etc/kpm.ini
(or
.IR $KPM_CONFIG )
for
.BR root ,
.BR ports_dir ,
and
.BR collections
priority order, and by reading CRUX's installed package database
.RI ( <root>/var/lib/pkg/db )
under a shared
.BR flock (2)
lock on
.IR <root>/var/lib/pkg .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\fR, \fBupdate \fR[\fIcollection\fR ...]
Concurrently synchronize all configured port collections (or only the named
collections) using a bounded worker pool.
Runs pre\-flight DNS and TCP reachability diagnostics before starting workers
unless
.B \-\-no\-netcheck
is passed, and cleanly handles
.B SIGINT
/
.B SIGTERM
cancellation.
.TP
.B \-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR, \fBlist \fR[\fIcollection\fR ...]
List available local ports under
.I ports_dir
in CRUX
.I <collection>/<port>
format (matching
.B ports \-l
and
.BR "kpm list \-\-ports" ).
Pass
.B \-\-collections
to display configured collection sync states instead.
.TP
.B \-d\fR, \fB\-\-diff\fR, \fBdiff \fR[\fIcollection\fR ...]
Compare local port versions parsed natively from
.B Pkgfile
recipes against installed package versions in
.IR <root>/var/lib/pkg/db ,
honoring
.B kpm.ini
collection priority order and numeric\-aware version comparison.
Prints a
.I "Collection  Name  Port  Installed"
table (including
.I MISSING
for installed packages absent from local ports) or
.IR "No differences found" .
.TP
.B \-s\fR, \fB\-\-search\fR, \fBsearch \fIquery\fR ...
Perform a fast local case\-insensitive substring search across port names,
relative paths, and
.B "# Description:"
headers, printing matches as
.IR "<collection>/<port> <version> - <description>" .
.TP
.B status
Inspect configured collections from
.I sources.list
without network I/O and print a table of collection name, protocol, destination
directory, and local sync status (including short Git HEAD commit and port count).
.TP
.B check
Validate
.I sources.list
and
.I sources.list.d/*.list
syntax and run pre\-flight
.IR /etc/resolv.conf ,
DNS, and TCP connectivity checks without modifying
.IR ports_dir .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " \fIn\fR"
Maximum number of concurrent collection sync workers (default:
.BR 4 ).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Path to the primary
.I sources.list
file (default:
.I $PORTS_CONFIG
or
.IR /etc/ports/sources.list ).
.TP
.B \-\-kpm\-config \fIpath\fR
Explicit path to
.BR kpm (8)
INI configuration file (default:
.I $KPM_CONFIG
or
.IR /etc/kpm.ini ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root " \fIdir\fR"
Override
.B [paths] root
from
.I kpm.ini
when reading
.IR var/lib/pkg/db .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-ports\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
Override
.B [paths] ports_dir
from
.I kpm.ini
(default:
.IR $PORTS_DIR ,
.IR $KPM_PORTS_DIR ,
.IR $KRYX_PORTS_DIR ,
or
.IR /usr/ports ).
.TP
.B \-\-collections
With
.BR \-l / list ,
show configured collection sync status (equivalent to
.BR "ports status" ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-netcheck
Skip pre\-flight DNS and TCP reachability checks before syncing.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit 0.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B ports
reads collection sources from
.I /etc/ports/sources.list
and optional drop\-in files matching
.IR /etc/ports/sources.list.d/*.list
(falling back automatically to legacy
.I /etc/gports/sources.list
if present).
Each non\-comment line has the format:
.RS
.PP
.nf
<protocol> <collection> <url> [destination_dir]
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KPM_CONFIG
Path to
.I kpm.ini
(shared with
.BR kpm (8)).
.TP
.B PORTS_CONFIG
Override default path to
.IR sources.list .
.TP
.B PORTS_DIR\fR, \fBKPM_PORTS_DIR\fR, \fBKRYX_PORTS_DIR
Override default local ports root directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ports/sources.list
Primary collection sources list.
.TP
.I /etc/ports/sources.list.d/*.list
Optional drop\-in collection definitions loaded in lexicographical order.
.TP
.I /etc/kpm.ini
Shared
.BR kpm (8)
INI configuration file.
.TP
.I <root>/var/lib/pkg/db
CRUX/kpm installed package database read under a shared
.BR flock (2)
lock during
.BR "ports \-d" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
ports check
ports \-u
ports \-u \-j 2 core opt
ports \-l
ports \-d
ports \-s ripgrep
ports status
kpm ports \-u
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kpm (8),
.BR kpm\-index (8),
.BR kryx\-src (8),
.BR pkginfo (8)
